# @req REQ-BOARD-VULKAN-SUBMIT-ADRENO
"""
# Board Vulkan — Adreno device submit/readback evidence

This requirement has no executable device provider or independent Turnip
comparison adapter yet. `backend_adreno.spl` explicitly leaves submit and
readback unimplemented. Hardware presence alone cannot supply these owners.

The previous body inspected `/sys/class/drm` and then constructed and walked
`adreno_minimal_submission()` entirely on the CPU. Its register address and
draw operands are documented placeholders. That operation is encoder-format
coverage, never a device submission, device readback, or cross-architecture
capture. The existing `adreno_cmdstream_encoder_pkt_header_spec.spl` retains
encoder unit coverage; it is not promoted to this system requirement.

Register a real framework skip while the provider is missing, rather than
returning an ordinary `"skip: ..."` string from a test body or accepting CPU
packet layout on a host with an msm device. The canonical skip owner records
an actual skipped result and its assurance policy rejects unsupported skips
under critical validation. This requirement earns no passing assertion.

Replace this registered skip only when a manifest-bound Adreno provider can
submit to the actual device, return device-origin readback, retain the board
and firmware identity, and compare captured boundaries with the independent
counterpart. A passing encoder or a device-presence probe is insufficient.

Tracking: doc/08_tracking/bug/board_vulkan_cross_arch_boundary_only_x86_64_proven_2026-08-11.md
"""

use std.spec.{describe, skip}

describe "board Vulkan Adreno device submit/readback":
    skip(
        "captures Adreno device submit/readback and independent counterpart boundaries",
        "Blocked: Adreno submit/readback provider and independent Turnip adapter are absent; hardware presence and CPU packet layout are insufficient. See board_vulkan_cross_arch_boundary_only_x86_64_proven_2026-08-11."
    )
